WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.047
The workbook uses three
words for populations,

2
00:00:03.047 --> 00:00:05.275
and each is a view of the one above it.

3
00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:08.650
The class says who is
authoritative and who owns access.

4
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.529
Worker type is the HR attribute
for the agency's own workers,

5
00:00:12.529 --> 00:00:16.725
and a partner person has none,
because there's no agency HR record.

6
00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:20.987
The persona is how Conditional Access
targets people, and for partners

7
00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:24.887
that's the Externals persona, which
must match the class one to one.

8
00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:28.362
The user type is where those
views can quietly diverge.

9
00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:32.672
The workbook's member baselines, such
as the compliant-device policies,

10
00:00:32.672 --> 00:00:36.178
exclude guests, so a partner
created as a member would fall

11
00:00:36.178 --> 00:00:39.538
into the internal baselines
and out of the partner ones.

12
00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:41.988
So partner persons are guests by default.

13
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:45.219
A member partner person
needs an exception record,

14
00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:47.980
with a reason, an approver
and a review date.
